## Claude Code vs Direct API Calls

**Always use Claude Code (`claude-fda -p`)** for automated tasks - it runs on {{USER_NAME}}'s Max subscription (flat rate). **Never suggest direct Anthropic API calls** (`anthropic` SDK, `curl` to Messages API) - those are pay-per-token and expensive.

This applies to: consolidation jobs, denoising, any headless Claude work. CC is the standard path.

**Default model:** Per `{{USER_CLAUDE_HOME}}/settings.json`, the main session and subagents run configured defaults. The Telegram daemon runs its own configured model per `{{MINERU_HOME}}/landline.json`. Concrete model choices live in `prompts/TECHNICAL.local.md`. {{USER_NAME}} is OK with using a more powerful model even for mundane tasks - no need to add extra model flags unless {{USER_PRONOUN_SUBJECT}} specifically and explicitly ask{{USER_VERB_S}} for a cheaper/faster model.

### When to Use Sub-Agents in Main Session

**Use the Agent tool for any code-heavy work in the main session:**
- PR investigations, CI failures, code tracing.
- Exploring large codebases or repos.
- Debugging across multiple files.
- Any task that requires reading/navigating many source files.

**Do not do code exploration manually** in the main session - it burns context tokens. Spawn a sub-agent instead.

