## When Jobs Go Silent

Two failure modes cause all cron jobs to stop delivering at once:

**Auth expiry (401).** Claude Code's auth token expires, making every headless `claude-fda -p` job fail with `401 Invalid authentication credentials` (or `Failed to authenticate: OAuth session expired and could not be refreshed`). The key-icon alert fires; confirm with `claude-fda -p 'say hi'`; recovery is restarting the Mac (or re-logging-in CC).

**Max budget cap ("session limit").** The Max subscription's session budget resets on a rolling schedule (the reset time varies and is printed in the error). Jobs that fire near the reset boundary can hit the cap and fail with `"You've hit your session limit"`. Symptom looks identical to auth expiry (burst of alerts, deliveries stop), but the fix is different: wait for the quota reset (no restart needed). To distinguish: check the job log for "session limit" / "resets" vs "401". Safe to re-run jobs after reset; `consolidate-daily-memories` has a date arg + idempotency guard (skips if the consolidated file already exists).

**No automatic catch-up, by design.** A failed run is not re-fired; the next scheduled cycle picks up on its own (daily jobs the next day, weekly jobs the next week), so a failure costs at most one cycle of coverage. Do not propose a re-run script for this; re-run a job by hand only when a specific day's output matters.

**Homebrew Python patch upgrades (silent break of venv-pinned + TCC-guarded launchd jobs).** Every `brew upgrade python@3.x` bumps the patch level and changes the interpreter's code signature. Two failure modes result: (1) venvs pinned to the old patch lose their linked stdlib and die on next launch - recreate the venv against the new binary; (2) launchd jobs that use AppleEvents (Notes/Contacts/etc.) lose their TCC "Automation" grant because macOS keys the grant on the binary signature, so the job silently fails with "Not authorized to send Apple events" (-1743). Policy: **launchd-invoked scripts that touch Notes/TCC use `/usr/bin/python3` (Apple stock, stable Apple-signed)** instead of `/opt/homebrew/bin/python3`. Which jobs are pinned this way on this install: `prompts/TECHNICAL.local.md`.

Google auth is layered and each layer fails independently:
- `gog` CLI OAuth expires on its own (~4 months); check `gog auth status`, fix via the `{{PERSONA_NAME_LOWER}}__gog-auth` skill.
- The claude.ai Calendar MCP connector needs re-auth via `claude mcp login "claude.ai Google Calendar"` in an interactive session when its own token lapses. (The Gmail MCP connector is retired per `prompts/GMAIL.md`, so a Gmail-MCP outage does not block anything - Gmail runs on the `gog` CLI's own OAuth, refreshed via the `{{PERSONA_NAME_LOWER}}__gog-auth` skill.)
- The Drive connector uses a separate login and often survives Gmail outages, which makes it a useful source-of-truth fallback mid-outage.

