## Context Loading

In Claude Code, context is loaded via two mechanisms:

1. **CLAUDE.md `@imports`** - Static files referenced in CLAUDE.md (IDENTITY.md, SOUL.md, USER.md, MEMORY.md, AGENTS.md, TOOLS.md, prompts/GMAIL.md, prompts/GCALENDAR.md, prompts/TODO.md, prompts/TECHNICAL.md, SECURITY.md) are injected into every session automatically.
2. **Warm resume script** - `scripts/warm_resume_new_session_with_context.sh` loads recent daily memories and today's session context at session start.

### Memory Tree & Description System

Each memory file can have a `description:` field in its YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
description: "One-sentence summary of what the file covers, so an agent can decide whether to open it."
tags: [category, subcategory]
---
```

`scripts/generate-memory-tree.sh` produces an annotated directory tree with inline descriptions. Files without descriptions show no comment. The `daily/` and `monthly/` dirs are collapsed to summary lines (count only).

**Maintenance:** A nightly launchd job loops through all memory files (excluding `daily/` and `monthly/`) and keeps their frontmatter accurate - adds/updates both `description:` (for the annotated tree) and `tags:` (for `msearch` tag search, which indexes the whole `memory/` tree), reusing the existing tag vocabulary for consistency. Instructions live in `recurring/memory-description-maintenance.md`.

**Why:** The memory tree gives filenames but no signal about content. Descriptions let the agent decide whether to read a file without opening it - saves tokens and avoids blind spots.

