## Directory Structure

High-level layout (run `ls {{MINERU_HOME}}/` for the full snapshot):

- `prompts/` - Always-loaded via CLAUDE.md @imports (GMAIL, GCALENDAR, TODO, TECHNICAL).
- `recurring/` - Instruction markdown for each cron job. Paused jobs keep their instruction files here; only their **outputs** are archived under `archive/paused-jobs/` (see `recurring/README.md`).
- `memory/` - `daily/` session logs + structured subfolders (a per-user namespace folder plus people, projects, places, faith, social, travel, lifestyle, recipes, events, monthly, archive/).
- `briefs_*/` - One output dir per recurring job.
- Telegram daemon - lives in its own repo (see `TOOLS.md` -> Telegram); the workspace keeps only `landline.json`, the `launchd/` plists (rendered from `engine/launchd/`), and `bin/restart-daemon.sh`.
- `browser/` - Playwright browser automation server (port 9471).
- `scripts/` - Trigger scripts, delivery helper, firewall, memory tooling.
- `bin/` - CLI tools symlinked to `{{USER_HOME}}/.local/bin` (msearch, gog-firewall, imsg-firewall, browser, and friends); also `restart-daemon.sh` and `imsg-named` (present but FORBIDDEN for reads - use `imsg-firewall`).
- `lib/` - Shared Python modules.
- `logs/` - Per-job rotating logs.
- `reports/` - Ad-hoc research artifacts.
- `cache/`, `inbox/`, `outbox/`, `creations/` - runtime state and scratch space.
- `app/` - {{PERSONA_NAME}} web-app source (its plist is in `launchd/`; if the web app is installed).
- `engine/`, `profiles/<name>/` (the `active` symlink), `launchd/`, `config/`: see CLAUDE.md "Editing this file".

